I don't have a strong feeling on which "quick fix" is better. The issue tha=
t makes it messy is it's hard to do uniformly, because each has its own wri=
nkle: CGV=3D>CVGV creates tosmabru if the CGV was initial, whereas CGV=3D>C=
V'V sometimes creates slinku'i or lujvo-shaped words, the latter of which i=
s a tcizbaga-type situation (and I know some BPFK members don't think that'=
s a problem).

mu'o mi'e durkavore


